## Concept and Decision

**Current concept and intended experience:**

Deckrush: Blitz is a fast-paced medieval fantasy deck-building game. Players build their own decks and use different card combinations to create strategies. I want the game to be easy to learn but still give players important choices during each turn. I also want the game to eventually support multiplayer.

**Design question or decision:**

The main question I was working on was what direction I wanted the gameplay to take and how I could make the game work as a multiplayer experience.

**Selected concept and alternatives kept:**

I decided to continue developing Deckrush: Blitz as a fast-paced deck-building game. I also explored different gameplay directions through the Workshop Idea Bank instead of immediately committing to one idea.

**Peer feedback that affected the decision, if received (otherwise say unavailable):**

I received feedback from the group I worked with during the Workshop Idea Bank. Their feedback gave me new ideas for how the gameplay could work and made me consider different directions for the game.

